(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the architecture, simulation solver modes \(Continuous, Discrete, Phasor\), and use cases of MATLAB/Simulink Simscape Electrical.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Simscape Electrical in MATLAB/Simulink:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Architectural Overview:) Tj
T*
(   Simscape Electrical \(incorporating legacy SimPowerSystems\) models physical multi-domain) Tj
T*
(   electrical networks using physical conserving ports \(voltage-current Kirchhoff connections\)) Tj
T*
(   seamlessly integrated with Simulink mathematical signal flow.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Powergui Block & Solver Modes:) Tj
T*
(   - Continuous Solver: Employs variable-step numerical integration algorithms \(ode45, ode23t,) Tj
T*
(   ode15s\). Ideal for high-precision simulation of non-linear analog transients and RLC networks.) Tj
T*
(   However, simulation speed drops drastically when modeling fast-switching PWM power converters) Tj
T*
(   due to zero-crossing events.) Tj
T*
(   - Discrete Solver: Discretizes the entire state-space system with a fixed sample time $T_s$) Tj
T*
(   \(typically 1 to 50 microseconds\) using Tustin \(bilinear\) or Backward Euler approximations.) Tj
T*
(   Converts dynamic differential equations into linear algebraic matrices solved in fixed) Tj
T*
(   execution intervals, providing 10x-50x faster execution and enabling real-time code generation) Tj
T*
(   for hardware controllers.) Tj
T*
(   - Phasor Solver: Replaces instantaneous sinusoidal differential equations with AC phasor) Tj
T*
(   algebraic equations at nominal frequency \(50/60 Hz\). Models macroscopic grid electromechanical) Tj
T*
(   oscillations, generator swing dynamics, and load flow without calculating microsecond sub-cycle) Tj
T*
(   waveforms, permitting high-speed simulation of national multi-machine power grids.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the principles, mathematical modeling, and operational applications of PSCAD/EMTDC in transmission system transients.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   PSCAD / EMTDC Simulation Suite:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Foundation \(H. W. Dommel's Algorithm\):) Tj
T*
(   EMTDC solves electromagnetic transients by applying the trapezoidal rule to discretize reactive) Tj
T*
(   transmission components into equivalent resistive companion circuits with parallel historical) Tj
T*
(   current sources:) Tj
T*
(   - Inductor \($v = L \\frac{di}{dt}$\): Approximated as equivalent resistance $R_{eq} =) Tj
T*
(   \\frac{2L}{\\Delta t}$ in parallel with history current source $I_h\(t - \\Delta t\) = i\(t - \\Delta) Tj
T*
(   t\) + \\frac{\\Delta t}{2L} v\(t - \\Delta t\)$.) Tj
T*
(   - Capacitor \($i = C \\frac{dv}{dt}$\): Approximated as $R_{eq} = \\frac{\\Delta t}{2C}$ in parallel) Tj
T*
(   with $I_h\(t - \\Delta t\) = -i\(t - \\Delta t\) - \\frac{2C}{\\Delta t} v\(t - \\Delta t\)$.) Tj
T*
(   This transforms the complex system of non-linear differential equations into an algebraic) Tj
T*
(   matrix equation $\\mathbf{G} \\mathbf{V}\(t\) = \\mathbf{I}\(t\) - \\mathbf{I}_h$, solved with fixed) Tj
T*
(   microsecond time steps \(typically 10-50 microseconds\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Transmission Line Wave Models:) Tj
T*
(   PSCAD implements frequency-dependent phase models \(J.Marti and Frequency-Dependent Phase) Tj
T*
(   Models\) that account for frequency-dependent conductor skin effect and ground return impedance,) Tj
T*
(   accurately simulating lightning strike surges, breaker restrikes, and high-voltage DC converter) Tj
T*
(   switching transients.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

