(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze finite element electromagnetic analysis \(FEA\) using ANSYS Maxwell for electrical machine design.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   ANSYS Maxwell Finite Element Analysis \(FEA\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Maxwell's Field Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   ANSYS Maxwell discretizes 2D and 3D electromagnetic domains into finite triangular or) Tj
T*
(   tetrahedral meshes, solving Maxwell's curl equations:) Tj
T*
(   $$\\nabla \\times \\left\( \\frac{1}{\\mu} \\nabla \\times \\mathbf{A} \\right\) = \\mathbf{J}_{ext} -) Tj
T*
(   \\sigma \\frac{\\partial \\mathbf{A}}{\\partial t}$$) Tj
T*
(   where $\\mathbf{A}$ is the magnetic vector potential and $\\mathbf{J}_{ext}$ is external current) Tj
T*
(   density.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Non-Linear Material Modeling:) Tj
T*
(   Incorporates non-linear B-H saturation curves and anisotropic core loss coefficients \(Steinmetz) Tj
T*
(   equations for hysteresis, eddy, and excess losses\) to optimize motor lamination geometry,) Tj
T*
(   minimize tooth saturation, and eliminate cogging torque in PMSM traction motors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
