(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Graduate Aptitude Test in Engineering \(GATE\): Examination structure, syllabus scope, and PSU recruitment dynamics.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The GATE Examination in Electrical Engineering:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Examination Structure:) Tj
T*
(   Administered annually on a rotational basis by the Indian Institutes of Technology \(IITs\) and) Tj
T*
(   the Indian Institute of Science \(IISc\). A 3-hour computer-based test consisting of 65 questions) Tj
T*
(   \(100 total marks\) comprising Multiple Choice Questions \(MCQ\), Multiple Select Questions \(MSQ\),) Tj
T*
(   and Numerical Answer Type \(NAT\) questions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Core Syllabus Breakdown:) Tj
T*
(   - Engineering Mathematics \(13 marks\): Linear algebra, calculus, differential equations, complex) Tj
T*
(   variables, probability, and numerical methods.) Tj
T*
(   - General Aptitude \(15 marks\): Verbal ability and numerical reasoning.) Tj
T*
(   - Electrical Engineering Core \(72 marks\): Electric Circuits, Electromagnetic Fields, Signals) Tj
T*
(   and Systems, Electrical Machines, Power Systems, Control Systems, Electrical & Electronic) Tj
T*
(   Measurements, Analog & Digital Electronics, and Power Electronics.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Career Gateways:) Tj
T*
(   - Direct PSU Recruitment: Maharatna utilities \(NTPC, PGCIL, BHEL, ONGC, IOCL, GAIL\) shortlist) Tj
T*
(   candidates directly from top GATE percentiles \(typically ranks 1 to 300\) for Group-A Executive) Tj
T*
(   Trainee posts.) Tj
T*
(   - Postgraduate Higher Education: GATE scores govern direct M.Tech/MS/Ph.D. admissions with MHRD) Tj
T*
(   research fellowships at IITs, IISc, and prestigious international universities \(NUS, NTU) Tj
T*
(   Singapore, TU Munich\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
