(   mandates periodic, comprehensive energy audits for all 'Designated Consumers' \(heavy) Tj
T*
(   energy-intensive industries: thermal plants, cement, fertilizers, steel, railways\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Four-Paper Examination Curriculum:) Tj
T*
(   - Paper 1: General Energy Management: Global energy scenarios, energy conservation act,) Tj
T*
(   financing, energy economics \(NPV, IRR, Payback Period\), and project management.) Tj
T*
(   - Paper 2: Energy Efficiency in Thermal Utilities: Boiler combustion efficiency, heat) Tj
T*
(   exchangers, steam traps, furnaces, cogeneration, and waste heat recovery.) Tj
T*
(   - Paper 3: Energy Efficiency in Electrical Utilities: Electric motors \(IE3/IE4 standards\), VFD) Tj
T*
(   applications, transformers, compressed air systems, cooling towers, and commercial) Tj
T*
(   HVAC/lighting.) Tj
T*
(   - Paper 4: Energy Performance Assessment \(Practical Case Studies\): Open-book numerical exam) Tj
T*
(   requiring full industrial energy audit balance calculations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Industrial Audit Methodology:) Tj
T*
(   Certified auditors measure electrical power profiles using portable power analyzers, identify) Tj
T*
(   thermodynamic and electrical losses, calculate specific energy consumption \(SEC\), and formulate) Tj
T*
(   cost-effective Energy Conservation Measures \(ECMs\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
