T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the engineering design challenge of Formula Student Electric / Formula Bharat EV, focusing on the High-Voltage Accumulator.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Formula Student Electric \(FSE\) Powertrain Engineering:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Competition Framework:) Tj
T*
(   Collegiate design competition where students design, build, and test a single-seat) Tj
T*
(   formula-style electric racecar evaluated across static \(Engineering Design, Cost, Business) Tj
T*
(   Plan\) and dynamic events \(Acceleration, Skidpad, Autocross, Endurance\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. High-Voltage Accumulator Pack Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Voltage Constraint: Tractive system voltage is capped at $600\\text{ V DC}$ nominal under) Tj
T*
(   Formula Student rules.) Tj
T*
(   - Cell Selection: High-discharge Lithium-ion cells \(typically pouch or cylindrical 21700 cells\)) Tj
T*
(   configured in series-parallel \(e.g. 144S2P delivering ~530V and 7-10 kWh\).) Tj
T*
(   - Safety Rules & Accumulator Management System \(AMS\):) Tj
T*
(   The AMS must monitor every individual cell voltage and cell temperature. If any cell voltage) Tj
T*
(   drops below 2.5V or exceeds 4.2V, or if temperature exceeds $60^\\circ\\text{C}$, the AMS must) Tj
T*
(   instantly open the Shutdown Circuit within 500 ms.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Safety Circuitry:) Tj
T*
(   Includes two normally open High Voltage Contactors, a Pre-Charge relay and resistor, an Inertia) Tj
T*
(   Switch, Emergency Stop switches, an Insulation Monitoring Device \(Bender IMD\), and a Tractive) Tj
T*
(   System Active Light \(TSAL\) providing visual safety indication.) Tj
