(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the working principles and calibration of a High-Voltage Differential Probe for power electronics measurements.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   High-Voltage Differential Probes:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. The Grounding Hazard:) Tj
T*
(   Standard oscilloscope BNC probe ground clips are connected directly to mains earth ground.) Tj
T*
(   Connecting a standard probe clip to an upper MOSFET source terminal in a half-bridge inverter) Tj
T*
(   creates a dead short circuit, destroying the oscilloscope and inverter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Differential Operation:) Tj
T*
(   A differential probe uses two balanced high-impedance attenuator inputs \($+$ and $-$\) connected) Tj
T*
(   to an internal precision instrumentation amplifier that subtracts the two signals \($V_{diff} =) Tj
T*
(   V_+ - V_-$\) while rejecting common-mode voltages up to thousands of volts \($> 1000\\text{ V}$\).) Tj
T*
(   The output is a safe, ground-referenced low-voltage signal fed to the oscilloscope.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
