/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the design of high-current power busbars and trace sizing on multi-layer PCBs using IPC-2152 standards.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   PCB Trace Current Capacity \(IPC-2152 Standard\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Trace temperature rise is governed by $I^2 R$ Joule heating balanced against thermal convection) Tj
T*
(   and radiation:) Tj
T*
(   $$I = k \\cdot \\Delta T^b \\cdot A^c$$) Tj
T*
(   where $A$ is trace cross-sectional area, $\\Delta T$ is allowable temperature rise \(typically) Tj
T*
(   $10^\\circ\\text{C}$ to $30^\\circ\\text{C}$\), and $k, b, c$ are empirical curve-fitting constants.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Design Rules: Internal layers require double the width of external layers due to lower thermal) Tj
T*
(   dissipation. High-current power electronic tracks \($> 30\\text{ A}$\) use heavy 2 oz or 3 oz) Tj
T*
(   copper foils, parallel copper busbars, or exposed solder-coated copper traces.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 14:) Tj
T*
ET
