(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the principles of motor current signature analysis \(MCSA\) for non-invasive induction motor fault detection.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Motor Current Signature Analysis \(MCSA\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Principle: Faults in an induction motor \(broken rotor bars, airgap eccentricity, bearing) Tj
T*
(   degradation\) modulate the motor airgap magnetic flux, inducing sideband frequency components in) Tj
T*
(   the stator line current.) Tj
T*
(   2. Broken Rotor Bar Signature: Broken bars produce characteristic sideband peaks around) Tj
T*
(   fundamental supply frequency $f_0$:) Tj
T*
(   $$f_{sb} = f_0 \(1 \\pm 2s\)$$) Tj
T*
(   where $s$ is motor slip. MCSA detects these sidebands using high-resolution FFT spectra of) Tj
T*
(   stator current without stopping the motor.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
