(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the principles of grounding grid resistance measurement using the Fall-of-Potential method.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Fall-of-Potential Method \(IEEE Std 81\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Measurement Setup: Consists of the ground electrode under test \($E$\), a remote current probe) Tj
T*
(   \($C$\) placed at distance $D$, and a potential probe \($P$\) placed between $E$ and $C$.) Tj
T*
(   2. The 61.8% Rule: A known AC current is injected between $E$ and $C$. The true resistance is) Tj
T*
(   measured when potential probe $P$ is placed at exactly 61.8% of the distance $D$ from $E$,) Tj
T*
(   where potential curves flatten out into the zero-resistance plateau between earth resistance) Tj
T*
(   spheres.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
