(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the working and applications of Variable Autotransformers \(Variacs\) in electrical laboratories.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Variable Autotransformers \(Variac\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Construction: Single continuous toroidal copper winding wound around a circular magnetic) Tj
T*
(   core, with an exposed polished carbon brush rotating along the winding surface.) Tj
T*
(   2. Functionality: Delivers smoothly adjustable, continuously variable AC output voltage from 0V) Tj
T*
(   to ~110% of input voltage without interrupting load current.) Tj
T*
(   3. Limitation: Lacks galvanic isolation between input and output, requiring isolation) Tj
T*
(   transformers during sensitive test procedures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
