(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the methodology of partial discharge \(PD\) testing in high-voltage cables and gas-insulated switchgear.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Partial Discharge \(PD\) Testing \(IEC 60270\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Mechanism: Localized dielectric breakdowns occurring within air voids or defects in) Tj
T*
(   high-voltage insulation that do not completely bridge the conductors.) Tj
T*
(   2. Detection: High-frequency current transformers \(HFCT\), capacitive coupling sensors, and) Tj
T*
(   ultra-high-frequency \(UHF\) antennas measure transient nanosecond electromagnetic pulses) Tj
T*
(   generated by discharge sparks, detecting insulation deterioration years before complete) Tj
T*
(   dielectric failure.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
