(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the engineering design of a regenerative DC electronic load for testing power supplies and batteries.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Regenerative Electronic Loads:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Traditional electronic loads dissipate power as heat into massive resistor banks and cooling) Tj
T*
(   fans.) Tj
T*
(   Regenerative Load Architecture: Uses an active bidirectional PWM inverter to sink DC power from) Tj
T*
(   the device under test, boost voltage, and invert the energy back into the facility's 415V AC) Tj
T*
(   mains grid with $> 92\\%$ efficiency, slashing electricity costs and cooling loads in test labs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
